            "review_title": "Review at Yu Shang Lou - Fine Chinese Cuisine 2",
            "review_text": "Geoff\nLeigh-on Sea, United Kingdom226 contributions\n0\nVery nice\nMar 2019 • Couples\nA lovely restaurant... I would say middle of the road as regards to pricing.. \nBut in my view we'll worth the money. Service very good. Very efficient.. And very polite.... \nFood quality very good. Was impressed with the freshness of all the food we ordered.. \nThe sweet and sour pork was a winner for me as it had no bones so it was so enjoyable to eat. And so tasty. \nThe green beans with minced pork. So tasty and the beans not over cooked had a nice bit of crunch\nChicken in black pepper sauce soft and succulent.. And again no bones... So you can enjoy each mouthful. Without haveing to pick out the bones. \n\nBean curd with peanuts beautiful. \nAnd the house special fried rice. A tag expensive but very very tasty. \nWe were both given a complimentary deaert which was mango in a cream sauce and it was so tasty not over sweet.. \nThis is a quality restaurant. Which reflects in the price of the food... But please don't be put of at the pricing.. As it is very fresh and tasty food cooked to order and comes to the table piping hot.. \nAre meal for two which included 5 plates of food. A couple of beers. And one orange juice including taxes and service charge was £45.00 and in all honesty this quality of food in England would have been about £120.00. \nSo yes to us it was a bargain and we will be coming back. \n\nYes to the tourist its definitely worth a vist and enjoy....\nRead more\nWritten March 12, 2019",
